    "end": "She was his best man.",
    "caption": "Mind the gap in the middle of that row.\n\nViolet: 2.6 million people, a 23-hour day, no moons, and nobody can see a newcomer until someone sits down beside them. Then they're simply there, as if they always had been. Every school keeps a bench by the gate for it, and most first days have a quiet hour. Zara's lasted a week. Josh only sat down to tie his shoe.\n\nI was invisible for my first two days here. A dog found me. We're still in touch.\n\n(The story goes that the 'buddy bench', where a lonely child sits so that someone will come and ask them to play, reached American playgrounds in 2013 through a second-grader in Pennsylvania who'd seen one in a brochure from Germany. On Violet, the bench does the rest.)\n\nWhen were you last the new one?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Zara's daughter started school on Monday. She was seen by ten.",
